What is Semiconductor Waste Recovery?
Semiconductor Waste Recovery refers to an integrated set of processes that capture, treat, and recycle hazardous chemicals, metal sludges, and solid residues generated throughout the semiconductor manufacturing lifecycle. By converting waste streams into reusable raw materials-such as reclaimed hydrofluoric acid, solvents, and precious metals-this approach not only mitigates environmental impact but also delivers significant cost savings for fab operators. The recovery workflow typically includes waste segregation, chemical neutralization, metal leaching, filtration, and the final re introduction of purified reagents into upstream process steps.
